Cage macOS guest: SSHFS source and relink materials

This distribution contains the complete SSHFS, GLib, GNU gettext and PCRE2
upstream source archives, the Cage SSHFS patch, installed Homebrew recipes and
their external patch/resource, and the exact static libraries and headers used
to link Cage's SSHFS helper. build.json records source URLs, SHA256 digests,
versions and the build toolchain. manifest.json binds all these files to the
final signed project/cage-sshfs executable. Receipts retain build identity
without the developer's personal filesystem paths.

Rebuild or modify SSHFS on an Apple Silicon Mac with Xcode command-line tools:

1. Obtain the external macFUSE 5.5.0 SDK from its official installer. It is not
   installed by these commands. The pinned image and package hashes are checked
   by the included extraction script. Set SOURCE to this extracted directory,
   and WORK to a new, empty absolute directory:

   mkdir -p "$WORK"
   curl -fL https://github.com/macfuse/macfuse/releases/download/macfuse-5.5.0/macfuse-5.5.0.dmg -o "$WORK/macfuse.dmg"
   bash "$SOURCE/cage/macos-fuse-media.sh" "$WORK/macfuse.dmg" "$WORK/fuse.pkg"
   pkgutil --expand-full "$WORK/fuse.pkg" "$WORK/sdk"

2. Relink using the frozen static libraries and headers:

   bash "$SOURCE/rebuild-macos-sshfs.sh" "$SOURCE" "$WORK/sdk/Core.pkg/Payload/usr/local" "$WORK/cage-sshfs"
   codesign --force --sign - "$WORK/cage-sshfs"

   No Homebrew installation or network access is needed for this compile step.
   To modify SSHFS, first extract upstream/sshfs.tar.gz, apply
   cage/sshfs-openwith.patch with patch -p1, edit the files, then pass that source
   directory as the fourth argument to rebuild-macos-sshfs.sh.

The helper dynamically loads the separately installed macFUSE runtime. macFUSE
must be available on the machine where it runs. Xcode, the macOS SDK and macFUSE
are external system/build prerequisites; they are not redistributed here.
Rebuilding with another compiler or replacing the Developer ID signature will
change the executable hash. The manifest describes the shipped executable.

To rebuild the static dependencies, the complete upstream archives are in
upstream/. The exact Homebrew install methods, configure/Meson flags, inline
source changes, and versions used for the installed bottles are preserved in
homebrew/{glib,gettext,pcre2}.rb. GLib's separate introspection resource and
hardcoded-paths patch are also included. With Homebrew and its recipe build
tools, copy these recipes to a local tap (Formula/ and Patches/ retain their
relative paths) and run:

   brew install --build-from-source your/local/pcre2
   brew install --build-from-source your/local/gettext
   brew install --build-from-source your/local/glib

The formula install methods list their build prerequisites. As with ordinary
Homebrew builds, these general-purpose tools and the other formula runtime
dependencies can be installed separately. The source archives and required
GLib patch/resource are frozen here; configure local source URLs if building
without network access. Replace dependencies/* with your rebuilt static
libraries/headers before relinking. The frozen originals are provided so users
can relink modified SSHFS immediately, without having to reproduce Homebrew's
bottle build environment.

